{1408}{Amtut can be released only if the person ending his life carries a heartstone. The Grayhills librarian has a specimen; return the Rathouse overdue book first. Ordinary heartstones also work.}
{1409}{Amtut promises to remain in his chamber. Ask Pollock about the night of the attack and secure his agreement, then obtain Mayor Gray's protection for the refuge. Return to Amtut to seal the agreement.}
{1410}{Amtut has died with a heartstone present. His soul is released. His remorse did not erase the lives he took, but his imprisonment is over.}
{1411}{Grayhills and Amtut have agreed to leave one another in peace. His chamber is a refuge, and he will stay away from the farms. His curse remains.}
{1412}{The mummy is dead and Grayhills considers itself saved. Without a heartstone at his death, Amtut's soul remains trapped in his remains.}
